{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1028797-the-eye-of-ahriman","id":1028797,"title":"The Eye of Ahriman","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-08T17:41:16-08:00","id":1028797,"title":"The Eye of Ahriman","content":"First edition Mage, in the Mysterium book, introduced an artifact called the Eye of Ahriman. It's 'a scarab-shaped amulet carved of an unknown black crystal colder than ice.' It comes alive when placed over a suitable mage's eye and destroys the existing eye, sinking its 'legs' into the mage's brain and becoming impossible to use. A suitable mage is one with Destiny 5. 'It will not deign to join with a less cosmically important individual.'<br /> <br /> The artifact's powers itself are cool, for the most part allowing control over Shadows, passive night vision and emulating various Death-like Shadow spells.<br /> <br /> In the backstory of the object, the Mysterium was unaware of its powers and use until 'a Scelestus wielding a sister Artifact attempted to steal the Eye and inadvertently tipped off its keepers to the means of activating its power.'<br /> <br /> My knowledge of Mage's first edition lore is pretty sparse, is the artifact or Ahriman referenced again anywhere? If not, do you think the 'sister Artifact' would also allow for control over Darkness, or would it allow for some other strangeness attuned to the concept of Ahriman? <br /> <br /> Has anyone used it in their games? If so, how did its story develop?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T05:46:29-08:00","id":1028980,"title":"","content":"I have absolutely no idea of what this Artifact is, but if it has a sister I'd have it bee the Eye of Ormahzd (spelling?), the good counterpart of Ahriman, that gives control over light and illumination.<br /> <br /> If it has to be connected to Ahriman still, then I'd let it have powers over the metaphorical shadows - illusions, hallucinations, concealments and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}